From: Chaos Ruler <zmelumian@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] SM8550: drop pcie_ports=compat so the Wi-Fi link powers off in sleep

With pcie_ports=compat no driver binds the PCIe root port (0000:00:00.0),
so it stays enabled in D0 through system sleep. pci_host_common_d3cold_possible()
then refuses D3cold even though ath12k is in D3hot, dw_pcie_suspend_noirq()
returns early, and qcom_pcie_suspend_noirq() takes the "link up" branch:
controller clocks, GDSC, PHY and its LDO rails all stay on. Verified on the
Thor: no "link up" print after any resume, only at boot.

With portdrv bound the root port goes to D3hot (pci_bridge_d3_possible() is
true on non-x86), the host sends PME_Turn_Off and deinits the controller
(clocks, PHY, regulators off, PERST asserted). That is deeper than Android's
L1ss/DRV sleep (OnePlus pci-msm.c msm_pcie_drv_suspend), which keeps the link.
---
--- a/projects/ROCKNIX/devices/SM8550/options
+++ b/projects/ROCKNIX/devices/SM8550/options
@@ -28,7 +28,7 @@
     KERNEL_MAKE_EXTRACMD=" $(get_kernel_make_extracmd)"

   # Kernel cmdline
-    EXTRA_CMDLINE="quiet rootwait console=tty0 allow_mismatched_32bit_el0 fw_devlink.strict=0 fw_devlink.sync_state=timeout pcie_ports=compat irqaffinity=0-2 cgroup.memory=nokmem,nosocket nosoftlockup usbcore.interrupt_interval_override=045e:028e:2 ufshcd_core.uic_cmd_timeout=3000 mem_sleep_default=s2idle vt.global_cursor_default=0 loglevel=1 systemd.show_status=false gpt"
+    EXTRA_CMDLINE="quiet rootwait console=tty0 allow_mismatched_32bit_el0 fw_devlink.strict=0 fw_devlink.sync_state=timeout irqaffinity=0-2 cgroup.memory=nokmem,nosocket nosoftlockup usbcore.interrupt_interval_override=045e:028e:2 ufshcd_core.uic_cmd_timeout=3000 mem_sleep_default=s2idle vt.global_cursor_default=0 loglevel=1 systemd.show_status=false gpt"

   # Bootloader to use (syslinux / u-boot)
     BOOTLOADER="qcom-abl"
